INT. CHURCH BELFRY - SNIPER NEST - DAWN

Stone arches. A cracked bell hangs silent. Through the slit, a ruined square below.

LT. VASILY PETRENKO whispers into a field phone. SPC. TANISHA GREER braces a rifle on a sandbag. PVT. LEO FONTAINE feeds a belt into a machine gun. CPL. HANNELORE WEISS hauls up an ammo crate. SGT. OBINNA ADEKUNLE-REID wedges the door with a pew. PVT. JUNE KOWALCZYK clutches a radio.

A shell whistles overhead. The tower shakes.

TANISHA
Contact left!

LEO
Where?

TANISHA
Left! Your other left!

VASILY
Sergeant, the door!

OBINNA
I'm holding it!

HANNELORE
(dropping the crate)
They're in the nave!

JUNE
Lieutenant, radio says pull back!

VASILY
To where?

JUNE
It doesn't say!

A boot hits the door. Wood splinters. Obinna braces both shoulders against it.

OBINNA
Anyone?

LEO
Firing!

The machine gun roars. Dust and cordite fill the belfry. Tanisha squeezes the trigger once, twice. A body falls in the square.

TANISHA
Down!

Silence. Then bells. The cracked bell, ringing on its own in the blast's echo.

They all stop. Look up.

HANNELORE
(softly)
It still rings.
